   The mind machines mailing list (mind-l[-request]@asylum.sf.ca.us) has
been discussing recently nootropics and cognitive-enhancing effects of
mind machines.  I haven't followed the discussion closely, but what I read
seems interesting.  I am including one representative message below (with
author's permission).
  If anybody has been following the discussion, could you post a review here?

Also, what other lists do you people read?
My finds, close to extropian interests, are: fringe <fringeware@io.com>
(probably the closest thing to extropian list I know), TAG list (topics on
Talented And Gifted children), CYBSYS (Cybernetics and system theory),
currently dormant World Future society, future-tech and Society of Mind lists,
agoric systems list, and, of course, exi-essay, altinst, cryonics and cypher-
punks.  And, yes, leri-l and general semantics lists.
   Anything else out there?  Could anybody give a review of their favorite
lists?

   Anyway, here's the promised post from mind-l:

