Hi, I tried most of these.  I was not too impressed with Piracetam, but I 
thought Hydergine was interesting.  One looks for more mental 
"brightness", a slight mood lift, clearer thinking, better attention, 
faster reactions.

HOWEVER ALL nootropics are only TEMPORARY.  They only work when you take 
'em.  Stop taking them and the effect rapidly declines.

What impresses me vastly (right now) is that all the positive effects of 
nootropics can be obtained PERMANENTLY by doing beta brainwave training, 
which is what I have been up to the last few months.  

The protocol is to suppress theta in the range 4-7 Hz, enhance beta at 
15-18 Hz and suppress high beta at 22-30 Hz.  The EEG Systems unit I have 
used is VERY effective in teaching this, and I use a "BrainTracer" unit 
at home to allow me to train whenever I have time (you need at least 6 
sessions to see any difference, and preferably 25 to really transform 
things).  I can only say that the effects of this training are DRAMATIC 
(I'm about to write up my experiences for MEGABRAIN REPORT - thinking of 
calling it "Welcome to the Church of EEG Training", because of my becoming 
a fundamentalist "prosletyser" for this).

The effects are (and this is not everything).  Better memory, better 
attention, better comprehension, better mental arithmetic, better 
concentration, lower anxiety (MUCH lower), cessation of nocturnal 
bruxism, better sex (you can focus much better!), more energy & drive, 
better mobilisation & motivation, more happiness, better coordination (I 
found this out by accident when I suddenly realised I was swatting flies 
with my hands - a thing I could not do before efficiently (GREAT benefit !).

So as you can see, I am pretty sold on this, because it's permanent, does 
not decay (or if I do something to make it decay, I can restore full 
functioning with one or two "booster" sessions).  It is the closest 
thing to "brain tuning" and really FULFILLS the promises implicit in 
Michael Hutchison's vision of psychotechnology as providing incredible 
cognitive enhancement.  Interestingly, because it is SO powerful, it can 
be dangerous, because for those who react to increased arousal with rage, 
paranoia or mania, it can cause these, because it actually DOES have a 
profound effect in resetting the arousal "set point" of the brain.  Since 
I rather like being quasi-manic, I love the effects.

Best to all,

Julian Isaacs


